    {
      "id": "clm:e9ad1ed6d4f31bceb26870b8857d2e553e17b1f5035ba9a7b7620a09a957c949",
      "text": "Five systematic reviews with meta-analysis of rhythmic auditory cueing, rhythmic auditory stimulation (RAS) or music-based interventions in Parkinson's disease (Ghai, Ye, Wang, Lee and Ko, and Li) each report a positive pooled effect on gait velocity or speed and on stride or step length. (high confidence)",
