    {
      "id": "clm:f6adb6fbe79257e57a5f63588cd609ed713fc9dcb0278471113f3bbf76e39e19",
      "text": "Meta-analyses of RAS and music-based interventions in Parkinson's disease differ on balance and timed up-and-go (TUG) mobility: Wang and colleagues and Lee and Ko report statistically significant pooled improvements (Berg Balance Scale and TUG for Wang and colleagues; TUG for Lee and Ko), whereas Ye and colleagues report no significant pooled difference for either, and Li and colleagues report a pooled balance effect that became nonsignificant after sensitivity analysis. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9053573/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9859027/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9366143/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12580135/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
