    {
      "id": "clm:3ed902fcd9a708f385cf9f3d534c109763fcb267bb2f17ac4f112195d6f0dd73",
      "text": "Meta-analyses differ on non-motor outcomes of music-based or arts-based interventions in Parkinson's disease: Lee and Ko report no significant pooled effect on quality of life (SMD = \u22120.68, p = 0.18), and Liu and colleagues' meta-analysis of 22 studies (928 participants) reports non-significant effects on quality of life, cognition and depressive symptoms, whereas a music-therapy meta-analysis of thirty-three studies including 3635 patients (searched from inception to 31 August 2026) reports significant improvements in depression, anxiety and life quality. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9859027/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13281054/",
        "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/43076026/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
