    {
      "id": "clm:3b71a3177309cf99f8a01659c9c4092e4d537822050c7dea6c6ef48e84911660",
      "text": "A systematic review of randomized controlled trials of music-based interventions for cognitive rehabilitation in Parkinson's disease, which analyzed three articles, concluded that the results showed no evidence of efficacy for cognitive outcomes, and a randomized trial of a group-based music intervention that enrolled forty-six patients (Pohl and colleagues) states that it does not support efficacy for immediate or lasting gains in dual-tasking, cognition, balance, or freezing of gait. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10415237/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7132435/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:017c64de77b2e85c2e5770d89a1985b610a6494c9f7819eeb00c374c6a5ec7cb",
        "ev:324acabf67afdaacfa280f18572b31f161e1699d2ea4a7dd35040a2390e3e21d",
        "ev:440c0b6ae2271916241a553c5d27978349e08c38f4f4ceacd730edc46d817236",
