      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6e654c1710f54b12584866ee4b090206fefaba31b0788c514dfb7bb5a8ce9323",
      "text": "A systematic review of active group-based performing arts interventions in Parkinson's disease (searches conducted in February 2020) included fifty-six studies reported in 67 publications with a total of 1531 people with PD; dance was studied most (38 studies), followed by 12 studies on singing, four on music therapy and two on theatrical interventions, and the authors state that no studies compared interventions from different performing arts modalities. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7547481/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1b57477e0fae19fb56b3fbe050b4223abeb1be26e45b1ed338df1d522f910d6b",
        "ev:5397afefd9526e5650901e652a7b7c024609ab8fc57607b068ca1bc7bdca7a9b",
        "ev:6c012b2868b3368fc027b5e7cfe07cfba0c3e776267301fa5b86aee143176331",
        "ev:a9e2d5cd8247da0e2eccf34a79b0b2b5bcd0cd23de7da78e2c22195c44324373"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1c1d7826ad995ee42c146d912bc22eaaa3f60d891e3d6a63cbdb4a82422a2908",
      "text": "Reviews and a patient-organisation page describe the creative-therapy evidence base in Parkinson's disease as limited by small samples and weak designs: Barnish and Barran list small sample sizes and the absence of control groups in over half of the included studies among the main methodological concerns, Irons and Sheffield report that most singing studies' methods were not rated highly due to small sample sizes, blinding and weak study design, and the American Parkinson Disease Association page states that most complementary therapies, which it lists as including singing, music therapy, dance therapy, theater and art therapy, have usually been studied only in small groups of people. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7547481/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12645629/",
        "https://www.apdaparkinson.org/article/music-therapy-parkinsons-disease/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:49ef4486ea14d118168d6edf2eb30760a3ee80cbb5d64a8db57f7cf59cbf0898",
        "ev:5397afefd9526e5650901e652a7b7c024609ab8fc57607b068ca1bc7bdca7a9b",
        "ev:a4ac02137217d86e86bcc2d6ae6e8ce142429857ec1230759b195df984caed47",
        "ev:af507925f986401b4d126939cb9ff9deb5e2dee7c4541f4d560fe876b5196902",
